---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
import { CONTACT } from '../../data/site';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Funerals we arrange', url: '/funeral-services/' },
  { name: 'Natural burial', url: '/funeral-services/natural-burial/' },
];
---

<Page
  title="Natural & Woodland Burial in East Lothian"
  heading="Natural burial"
  description="Green and woodland burial arranged from Dunbar: biodegradable coffins, no embalming, and burial grounds across East Lothian and the Borders."
  standfirst="A funeral that leaves nothing behind that will not return to the ground."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <p>
    Natural burial — also called green or woodland burial — means burial in a way that
    lets everything break down naturally. No embalming, a fully biodegradable coffin or
    shroud, no plastics or metals, and usually a tree or a meadow rather than a headstone.
  </p>

  <p>
    Families choose it for different reasons. Some feel strongly about the environment.
    Some simply prefer the idea of a wood or a wildflower meadow to a row of polished
    granite. Some like that the grave will, in time, become part of the landscape rather
    than something needing upkeep.
  </p>

  <h2>What makes a burial natural</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>No embalming.</strong> Embalming fluid is a preservative and does not belong
      in a natural burial ground. We care for the person by refrigeration instead, which
      is what we do for most funerals anyway.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A biodegradable coffin.</strong> Willow, bamboo, banana leaf, pandanus,
      recycled cardboard, or a simple shroud.{' '}
      <a href="/coffins/">See the range</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Natural clothing.</strong> Cotton, wool or linen rather than synthetics.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A living memorial.</strong> A tree, or wildflowers, or nothing at all —
      most natural burial grounds do not permit conventional headstones.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The coffins</h2>
  <p>
    We supply the full Ecoffins range. They are handwoven from fast-growing renewable
    materials — willow, bamboo, pandanus and banana leaf — with no plastic, no metal, no
    screws and no staples. The cardboard coffins are made in the UK from more than 70%
    recycled material and can be decorated, painted or written on, which some families
    find helps enormously, particularly children.
  </p>
  <p>
    They are entirely suitable for cremation too, if you want the coffin to be natural
    without the burial being.{' '}
    <a href="/coffins/">See the whole range</a>.
  </p>

  <Callout title="A natural coffin in an ordinary cemetery">
    <p>
      You do not have to use a dedicated natural burial ground to have a natural coffin.
      Many families choose a willow or cardboard coffin for a conventional burial or
      cremation in their own local cemetery. It is a perfectly ordinary request and we
      arrange it often.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>Where</h2>
  <p>
    There are natural burial grounds within reach of East Lothian and the Borders, and
    some council cemeteries have areas set aside for green burial. Sites open and change
    their rules from time to time, so we keep a current list — with what each one allows,
    what it costs and how to visit — in our{' '}
    <a href="/directory/cemeteries/">cemetery directory</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Every site has its own rules about coffins, memorials, flowers and what may be placed
    on a grave. We will check the detail with the site before anything is arranged so
    there are no surprises on the day.
  </p>

  <h2>What the day is like</h2>
  <p>
    Usually simpler and more informal than a conventional burial. Services are often held
    at the graveside in the open air. Family frequently carry the coffin, and sometimes
    help to fill the grave — which sounds daunting written down, and which many people
    find is the part they are most glad they did.
  </p>

  <h2>What it costs</h2>
  <p>
    Natural burial is often comparable to conventional burial, sometimes less. Woven
    coffins can cost more than a basic wooden one; cardboard costs considerably less.
    Burial ground fees vary. Our own fee is on our{' '}
    <a href="/funeral-costs/standardised-price-list/">Standardised Price List</a> and we
    will give you a full written estimate.
  </p>

  <Callout tone="accent">
    <p>
      To talk about a natural burial, telephone{' '}
      <a href={CONTACT.phoneHref} class="font-semibold">{CONTACT.phone}</a>.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>Related</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/coffins/">Coffins, including the full eco range</a></li>
    <li><a href="/guides/natural-and-eco-friendly-funerals/">Guide to eco-friendly funerals</a></li>
    <li><a href="/funeral-services/burial/">Conventional burial</a></li>
  </ul>
</Page>
